1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,510
A clogged toilet always seems to happen at

2
00:00:02,520 --> 00:00:04,318
the worst possible moment.

3
00:00:04,610 --> 00:00:06,492
The good news is that most of the

4
00:00:06,502 --> 00:00:08,768
time you can clear it yourself in about

5
00:00:08,778 --> 00:00:13,212
ten minutes, with no plumber and no harsh
chemicals.

6
00:00:14,176 --> 00:00:16,604
Here are the seven steps, and what to

7
00:00:16,614 --> 00:00:18,448
do if nothing works.

8
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:20,105
WikiTube.

9
00:00:20,338 --> 00:00:22,555
Whatever it is, here's how.

10
00:00:22,833 --> 00:00:25,470
Most toilet clogs sit in the first bend

11
00:00:25,480 --> 00:00:28,071
of the drain, just out of sight, and

12
00:00:28,081 --> 00:00:30,056
they are made of too much paper or

13
00:00:30,066 --> 00:00:32,271
something that should never have been
flushed.

14
00:00:32,934 --> 00:00:35,954
That is why pressure, soap and a simple

15
00:00:35,964 --> 00:00:37,658
cable are usually enough.

16
00:00:38,460 --> 00:00:40,981
We will start with the gentlest method and

17
00:00:40,991 --> 00:00:43,129
work up, so you never do more than

18
00:00:43,139 --> 00:00:44,160
you need to.

19
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:46,035
Here is what you will need.

20
00:00:46,488 --> 00:00:47,881
A flange plunger.

21
00:00:48,241 --> 00:00:49,866
A pair of rubber gloves.

22
00:00:50,529 --> 00:00:51,549
Dish soap.

23
00:00:52,212 --> 00:00:54,116
A bucket of hot tap water.

24
00:00:54,569 --> 00:00:57,006
A toilet auger for the stubborn cases.

25
00:00:57,367 --> 00:00:59,619
And a few old towels for the floor.

26
00:01:00,167 --> 00:01:01,257
Step one.

27
00:01:02,059 --> 00:01:05,553
If the bowl is filling up, do not flush
again.

28
00:01:06,517 --> 00:01:09,316
A second flush sends a full tank, at

29
00:01:09,326 --> 00:01:11,543
least a gallon and a half of water,

30
00:01:11,567 --> 00:01:14,260
into a bowl that has nowhere to drain.

31
00:01:15,410 --> 00:01:17,443
Lift the lid off the tank and push

32
00:01:17,453 --> 00:01:20,413
the rubber flapper down over the hole at
the bottom.

33
00:01:20,867 --> 00:01:23,594
That stops more water from entering the
bowl.

34
00:01:23,955 --> 00:01:26,441
Then reach behind the toilet and turn the

35
00:01:26,451 --> 00:01:29,469
shut-off valve clockwise until it stops.

36
00:01:29,923 --> 00:01:32,154
Now the water level cannot rise, and you

37
00:01:32,164 --> 00:01:33,753
can work without a flood.

38
00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:35,356
Step two.

39
00:01:36,158 --> 00:01:38,830
Lay old towels or newspaper around the
base

40
00:01:38,840 --> 00:01:39,803
of the toilet.

41
00:01:40,466 --> 00:01:42,696
Pull on a pair of rubber gloves, and

42
00:01:42,706 --> 00:01:44,563
open a window if you can.

43
00:01:45,365 --> 00:01:47,315
If the bowl is full to the brim,

44
00:01:47,374 --> 00:01:49,604
bail some water into a bucket until it

45
00:01:49,614 --> 00:01:51,146
is about half full.

46
00:01:51,809 --> 00:01:54,130
You want enough water to cover the
plunger,

47
00:01:54,154 --> 00:01:56,417
but not enough to splash over the rim.

48
00:01:56,967 --> 00:01:58,023
Step three.

49
00:01:58,314 --> 00:02:00,789
Use a flange plunger, the kind with a

50
00:02:00,799 --> 00:02:03,375
soft rubber sleeve sticking out of the
cup.

51
00:02:04,340 --> 00:02:07,244
A flat sink plunger cannot seal the curved

52
00:02:07,254 --> 00:02:08,669
drain of a toilet.

53
00:02:09,332 --> 00:02:11,400
Run the plunger under hot water for a

54
00:02:11,410 --> 00:02:13,325
minute so the rubber softens.

55
00:02:13,871 --> 00:02:16,381
For an even tighter seal, smear a little

56
00:02:16,391 --> 00:02:18,979
petroleum jelly around the rim of the cup.

57
00:02:19,525 --> 00:02:21,303
Lower it in at an angle to let

58
00:02:21,313 --> 00:02:23,997
the air escape, then fit the sleeve into

59
00:02:24,007 --> 00:02:25,028
the drain hole.

60
00:02:25,993 --> 00:02:29,048
Make your first push slow and gentle, so

61
00:02:29,058 --> 00:02:31,948
trapped air does not blast water back at
you.

62
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:33,614
Step four.

63
00:02:34,277 --> 00:02:36,728
Keep the seal and pump the handle straight

64
00:02:36,738 --> 00:02:39,976
up and down, fifteen to twenty times.

65
00:02:40,639 --> 00:02:44,390
Push firmly, but pull just as hard,
because

66
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:46,408
the suction does half the work.

67
00:02:46,862 --> 00:02:49,220
The cup must stay under water the whole

68
00:02:49,230 --> 00:02:51,496
time, so top up the bowl from your

69
00:02:51,506 --> 00:02:53,548
bucket if the level gets low.

70
00:02:54,350 --> 00:02:57,045
On the last stroke, yank the plunger up

71
00:02:57,055 --> 00:02:58,900
sharply to break the seal.

72
00:02:59,563 --> 00:03:02,316
If the water rushes down the drain, the

73
00:03:02,326 --> 00:03:03,776
clog has moved.

74
00:03:04,068 --> 00:03:07,297
If nothing changes, repeat the whole round
two

75
00:03:07,307 --> 00:03:10,220
or three more times before moving on.

76
00:03:10,767 --> 00:03:11,881
Step five.

77
00:03:12,242 --> 00:03:14,333
Squirt about half a cup of dish soap

78
00:03:14,343 --> 00:03:15,387
into the bowl.

79
00:03:16,352 --> 00:03:17,512
No dish soap?

80
00:03:18,476 --> 00:03:21,935
Shampoo or liquid hand soap works the same
way.

81
00:03:22,737 --> 00:03:25,340
Fill a bucket with hot tap water, hot

82
00:03:25,350 --> 00:03:29,818
but never boiling, because boiling water
can crack porcelain.

83
00:03:30,969 --> 00:03:33,107
Pour it in from waist height, so the

84
00:03:33,117 --> 00:03:35,403
weight of the water pushes on the clog.

85
00:03:36,205 --> 00:03:38,633
Wait fifteen to twenty minutes while the
soap

86
00:03:38,643 --> 00:03:40,012
lubricates the pipe.

87
00:03:40,373 --> 00:03:42,267
If the water level has dropped while you

88
00:03:42,277 --> 00:03:45,425
waited, that is a very good sign: the

89
00:03:45,435 --> 00:03:47,942
clog is already letting water through.

90
00:03:48,906 --> 00:03:52,054
Then plunge again, and most stubborn clogs
give

91
00:03:52,064 --> 00:03:53,271
up at this point.

92
00:03:53,833 --> 00:03:55,051
Step six.

93
00:03:55,412 --> 00:03:57,814
For a clog that still will not move,

94
00:03:57,873 --> 00:04:01,657
use a toilet auger, also called a closet
auger.

95
00:04:02,203 --> 00:04:05,662
Its rubber sleeve protects the porcelain
from scratches.

96
00:04:06,209 --> 00:04:08,950
The cable is about three feet long, enough

97
00:04:08,960 --> 00:04:12,036
to reach any clog inside the toilet
itself.

98
00:04:12,838 --> 00:04:14,999
Rest the curved end in the drain and

99
00:04:15,009 --> 00:04:18,236
feed the cable in by turning the crank
clockwise.

100
00:04:18,527 --> 00:04:21,396
When you feel resistance, keep cranking
gently to

101
00:04:21,406 --> 00:04:23,646
break the clog apart or hook it.

102
00:04:24,007 --> 00:04:26,771
Then wind the cable back out slowly and

103
00:04:26,781 --> 00:04:29,184
drop whatever comes up into the bucket.

104
00:04:29,733 --> 00:04:30,777
Step seven.

105
00:04:31,579 --> 00:04:34,367
Turn the shut-off valve back on and let

106
00:04:34,377 --> 00:04:35,630
the tank refill.

107
00:04:36,432 --> 00:04:38,733
Take the lid off and keep one hand

108
00:04:38,743 --> 00:04:41,180
near the flapper, ready to close it.

109
00:04:41,727 --> 00:04:44,375
Flush once and watch the bowl empty with

110
00:04:44,385 --> 00:04:45,650
a strong swirl.

111
00:04:46,196 --> 00:04:49,205
If the water rises instead, close the
flapper

112
00:04:49,215 --> 00:04:51,780
right away and go back to the auger.

113
00:04:52,582 --> 00:04:55,254
Then flush three or four sheets of toilet

114
00:04:55,264 --> 00:04:58,386
paper as a final test: if they vanish,

115
00:04:58,561 --> 00:05:00,754
the drain is truly clear.

116
00:05:01,417 --> 00:05:03,961
Finish by rinsing the plunger and auger in

117
00:05:03,971 --> 00:05:07,642
the clean flush water, then disinfect
them, the

118
00:05:07,652 --> 00:05:09,868
floor and the handle.

119
00:05:10,433 --> 00:05:11,419
Still stuck?

120
00:05:12,569 --> 00:05:14,684
Before you give up, there are two more

121
00:05:14,694 --> 00:05:16,121
things worth trying.

122
00:05:16,482 --> 00:05:18,315
The first one is time.

123
00:05:18,978 --> 00:05:22,312
A paper clog softens by itself, so leave

124
00:05:22,322 --> 00:05:24,239
the soap and hot water in the bowl

125
00:05:24,249 --> 00:05:27,348
overnight, and plunge again in the
morning.

126
00:05:28,498 --> 00:05:30,694
The second one is a wet and dry

127
00:05:30,704 --> 00:05:33,863
shop vacuum, if you own one, and never

128
00:05:33,873 --> 00:05:35,835
a regular household vacuum.

129
00:05:36,381 --> 00:05:39,053
Vacuum the water out of the bowl, wrap

130
00:05:39,063 --> 00:05:41,177
an old towel around the hose to seal

131
00:05:41,187 --> 00:05:43,673
the drain, and let the suction pull the

132
00:05:43,683 --> 00:05:44,948
clog back out.

133
00:05:46,098 --> 00:05:48,886
As for baking soda and vinegar, the fizz

134
00:05:48,896 --> 00:05:51,766
looks impressive, but on a solid clog it

135
00:05:51,776 --> 00:05:55,214
does far less than soap, hot water and

136
00:05:55,224 --> 00:05:56,604
a good plunger.

137
00:05:57,167 --> 00:05:59,699
Sometimes the problem is not in your
toilet

138
00:05:59,709 --> 00:06:02,100
at all, and that is when you stop

139
00:06:02,124 --> 00:06:03,389
and call a plumber.

140
00:06:03,750 --> 00:06:07,106
Sign number one: when you flush, water
comes

141
00:06:07,116 --> 00:06:09,345
up in the shower or the bathtub.

142
00:06:10,309 --> 00:06:13,782
Sign number two: several drains in the
house

143
00:06:13,792 --> 00:06:16,508
are slow or gurgling at the same time.

144
00:06:17,055 --> 00:06:19,355
Both mean the blockage is in the main

145
00:06:19,365 --> 00:06:22,731
sewer line, far beyond the reach of a
plunger.

146
00:06:23,881 --> 00:06:26,809
Sign number three: you know a hard object

147
00:06:26,819 --> 00:06:30,974
went down, like a toy, a toothbrush or a
phone.

148
00:06:31,637 --> 00:06:33,691
Forcing it can wedge it deeper.

149
00:06:34,052 --> 00:06:37,525
And sign number four: the same toilet
clogs

150
00:06:37,535 --> 00:06:40,102
every few days, which points to a deeper

151
00:06:40,112 --> 00:06:42,317
problem that a pro should look at.

152
00:06:42,867 --> 00:06:46,976
Finally, here is how to never need this
video again.

153
00:06:47,638 --> 00:06:50,752
Only two things belong in a toilet: toilet

154
00:06:50,762 --> 00:06:53,013
paper and human waste.

155
00:06:53,676 --> 00:06:56,765
Wipes, even the ones sold as flushable, do

156
00:06:56,775 --> 00:06:58,713
not break down like paper.

157
00:06:59,376 --> 00:07:01,990
Put them in the trash, along with cotton

158
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:05,029
pads, dental floss and paper towels.

159
00:07:05,576 --> 00:07:07,737
When you use a lot of paper, flush

160
00:07:07,747 --> 00:07:11,868
twice: once halfway through, and once at
the end.

161
00:07:12,833 --> 00:07:15,412
If you have young children, a simple lid

162
00:07:15,422 --> 00:07:17,894
lock keeps toys out of the bowl.

163
00:07:18,347 --> 00:07:20,497
And keep that flange plunger next to the

164
00:07:20,507 --> 00:07:24,256
toilet, so the next clog is a two-minute
job.

165
00:07:24,800 --> 00:07:27,681
Now, the mistakes that turn a small clog

166
00:07:27,691 --> 00:07:29,280
into a big problem.

167
00:07:30,245 --> 00:07:34,519
One, flushing again and again, which is
how bathrooms

168
00:07:34,529 --> 00:07:35,167
flood.

169
00:07:36,317 --> 00:07:39,683
Two, pouring in chemical drain cleaner.

170
00:07:40,230 --> 00:07:43,041
It rarely works on toilets, it can damage

171
00:07:43,051 --> 00:07:45,781
the pipes, and if you plunge afterwards it

172
00:07:45,791 --> 00:07:47,496
can splash onto your skin.

173
00:07:48,461 --> 00:07:52,431
Three, using boiling water, which can
crack the bowl.

174
00:07:52,977 --> 00:07:55,789
And four, poking around with a wire coat

175
00:07:55,799 --> 00:07:59,084
hanger, which scratches the porcelain for
good.

176
00:07:59,633 --> 00:08:01,745
Let's run through it one more time.

177
00:08:02,036 --> 00:08:03,255
Stop the water.

178
00:08:03,430 --> 00:08:04,880
Protect the floor.

179
00:08:05,427 --> 00:08:07,945
Seal the drain with a flange plunger.

180
00:08:08,236 --> 00:08:10,046
Plunge in a steady rhythm.

181
00:08:10,848 --> 00:08:13,065
Add dish soap and hot water.

182
00:08:13,867 --> 00:08:15,225
Bring in the auger.

183
00:08:15,585 --> 00:08:17,918
Then test the flush and clean up.

184
00:08:18,279 --> 00:08:21,029
If it still will not clear, give it a
night.

185
00:08:21,576 --> 00:08:24,710
If other drains are backing up too, call a
plumber.

186
00:08:25,001 --> 00:08:28,344
And from now on, wipes go in the trash.

187
00:08:28,900 --> 00:08:32,104
That's how you unclog a toilet without
calling a plumber.

188
00:08:33,068 --> 00:08:36,170
If this saved your day, subscribe to
WikiTube

189
00:08:36,180 --> 00:08:38,910
for a new how-to every day, and tell

190
00:08:38,920 --> 00:08:40,605
us in the comments what you want us

191
00:08:40,615 --> 00:08:42,053
to explain next.

192
00:08:42,167 --> 00:08:43,327
That's WikiTube.

193
00:08:43,618 --> 00:08:45,939
Whatever it is, here's how.
